4. Technical Architecture
plain
School PC (Windows)
    └── Your Sync Agent (C# or Python)
            └── Reads SA-SAMS .mdb (C:\EDUSOLSAMS\Data\*.mdb)
            └── POSTs learner/subject data to your API
            └── Downloads project/mark updates from cloud

Your Cloud (Firebase / Supabase / AWS)
    └── PostgreSQL DB
    └── Node.js / Python API
    └── WhatsApp Business API (via Twilio or 2Chat or direct Meta API)
    └── Parent web app (React/Vue, mobile-first)
    └── Teacher web app (desktop + tablet friendly)

Payment: Paystack or Ozow integration
The .mdb read: Use pyodbc or mdbtools to query the Access database. SA-SAMS tables are relatively predictable — you'll mainly need Learner, Subject, Grade, Class, Educator tables. The agent should run on a schedule (e.g., nightly sync).
5. Pricing for Primary Schools
Primary schools are price-sensitive. Don't compete with iSAMS (R80k–R200k/year). 
Table
Tier	Price	Learners	Features
Starter	R499/month	Up to 300	SA-SAMS sync, project alerts, parent WhatsApp, mark capture
Standard	R999/month	Up to 800	+ Fee statements, online payments, multi-teacher accounts
Premium	R1,499/month	Unlimited	+ Custom branding, priority support, advanced reports
Plus: Once-off setup fee of R2,500–R5,000 per school (covers agent installation, training, and initial SA-SAMS mapping).
Your R1M path:
80 schools × R999/month average × 12 months = R959,000
Plus setup fees: 40 new schools/year × R3,500 = R140,000
Total: ~R1.1M
80 primary schools in South Africa is a tiny slice of the market. There are over 12,000 public primary schools.
6. Go-to-Market from Bloemfontein
Phase 1: Bloemfontein Proof (Months 1–3 after launch)
Target 5–10 primary schools in Bloem. Start with ones you have a connection to.
Offer 3 months free in exchange for being a case study and allowing you to film a 2-minute testimonial from the principal.
Focus on the "project panic" story. Film a parent describing the Sunday-night stress before, and the calm after.
Get a teacher to demo posting a project in 30 seconds.
Phase 2: Free State Expansion (Months 4–6)
Use testimonials to approach schools in Welkom, Kroonstad, Bethlehem.
The Free State Department of Education is smaller and more accessible than Gauteng/Western Cape. Provincial buy-in is possible.
Attend one SGB (School Governing Body) conference or principals' meeting.
Phase 3: National (Month 6+)
Sell via WhatsApp and Facebook Groups: "Primary School Principals South Africa," "SGB Members," "Teachers SA."
Run a simple landing page: nopanicprojects.co.za (or similar) with a 60-second video.
Offer a 14-day free trial where you remotely install the sync agent via AnyDesk.
Sales motion: Principals buy this, not IT departments. Your pitch is emotional: "How many angry parents have called you because their child 'forgot' about a project due tomorrow?"
